                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b7b6e218-076a-3d1f-8cff-bf698f824081",
                        "entry_id": "87618348-905f-363c-921e-bf065a988d17",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Person mit einer weißen Hautfarbe"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c4e1e5f-8ee1-4429-9d37-2d5fbbb31b4f",
                                "sense_id": "b7b6e218-076a-3d1f-8cff-bf698f824081",
                                "text": "Ergib dich Bleichgesicht!"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "47c7f2ff-0a69-483d-8de5-edfa126cacc9",
                        "source_entry_id": "87618348-905f-363c-921e-bf065a988d17",
                        "source_sense_id": "b7b6e218-076a-3d1f-8cff-bf698f824081",
                        "source_sense_description": "Person mit einer weißen Hautfarbe",
                        "target_lang_word": "paleface",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "paleface",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bae0e18c-4578-3f51-97fe-5ce7effbf02e",
                                        "entry_id": "39583f8b-7d5a-3e02-a90a-dbcf0e88db13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A white person, a person of European descent, particularly in Native American contexts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "ethnic",
                                            "offensive",
                                            "slur"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5bba2db-fbb6-41b5-b9b8-ed6f00b03c48",
                                                "sense_id": "bae0e18c-4578-3f51-97fe-5ce7effbf02e",
                                                "text": "Dere is Great Wicked Spirit, too... Heart grow hard. Great pleasure was to kill pale-face. Dat feeling last, Blossom, till I see you. Feel like fader to you, and don't want your scalp... Still want all udder pale-face scalp. Want Bourdon scalp much as any."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83ace447-716f-4196-b012-1f908ba7f34f",
                                                "sense_id": "bae0e18c-4578-3f51-97fe-5ce7effbf02e",
                                                "text": "The hearts of the palefaces would not thrill to these superstitions of the red men, though we spoke of them in the centre of the haunted region."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93599545-502d-4aee-82d8-499e048d530b",
                                                "sense_id": "bae0e18c-4578-3f51-97fe-5ce7effbf02e",
                                                "text": "The dusky hunters \"guyed\" the palefaces who could not do as well as they with their primitive weapons, even though the fire spouted from the iron tubes and the balls that could not be seen by the eye carried death farther than did the missiles launched by the natives."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2437f5be-fb23-4a6b-8638-6dc966dd6cb4",
                                                "sense_id": "bae0e18c-4578-3f51-97fe-5ce7effbf02e",
                                                "text": "\"Yes me big paleface—me come long way toward setting sun—go cross Big Water—go Buckskin—Siwash—chase cougar.\" The cougar, or mountain lion, is a Navajo god and the Navajos hold him in as much fear and reverence as do the Great Slave Indians the musk-ox."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9559c48b-f72b-4505-8062-c07098a3535b",
                                                "sense_id": "bae0e18c-4578-3f51-97fe-5ce7effbf02e",
                                                "text": "High Jack had been drinking too much rum ever since we landed in Boca. You know how an Indian is—the palefaces fixed his clock when they introduced him to firewater."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d05571c4-a9e6-4aa6-ab2c-0a9227f43628",
                                                "sense_id": "bae0e18c-4578-3f51-97fe-5ce7effbf02e",
                                                "text": "Some Blackfeet Indians, with a taste and a respect for Nature that shames the paleface, have protested to the Secretary of the Interior[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e725637-e5ba-42f6-a79f-bb0e17d02428",
                                                "sense_id": "bae0e18c-4578-3f51-97fe-5ce7effbf02e",
                                                "text": "Speed is whitey's drug, from the palefaces who cook it to the Caspers who deal it to the ofay vanilla wafers who snort or spike it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e1124fa1-db0f-499c-a568-e99bbd53cc26",
                        "source_entry_id": "87618348-905f-363c-921e-bf065a988d17",
                        "source_sense_id": "b7b6e218-076a-3d1f-8cff-bf698f824081",
                        "source_sense_description": "Person mit einer weißen Hautfarbe",
                        "target_lang_word": "visage pâle",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "visage pâle",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5da0bd60-145b-320b-ad68-6414f60cd70a",
                                        "entry_id": "53256870-647d-3f91-87a2-4a2428ce654b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Blanc d’origine européenne, appellation prétendument utilisée par les Amérindiens."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Folklore"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d4aac85-7197-4a69-9b36-c34ee84e5044",
                                                "sense_id": "5da0bd60-145b-320b-ad68-6414f60cd70a",
                                                "text": "Dès mon arrivée là-bas, j’ai prévenu Léonard, mon chef (la main sur le cœur, genre visage pâle rencontre peaux-rouges) […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "703d001d-509f-42df-823a-4e2dbaaf0df1",
                                                "sense_id": "5da0bd60-145b-320b-ad68-6414f60cd70a",
                                                "text": "Et Héloïse, ou Ludivine, ou Rita, ou encore Lesly, de me refiler sa carte ou son numéro de portable avant de décamper comme une Visage Pâle poursuivie par une meute de Peaux-Rouges."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
